WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Many microbes are difficult to grow in the lab, so we study the DNA present in the sample instead.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Select the anaerobic digestion goal and load the provided dataset.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
See the file details before any microbial analysis is shown.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Check the number of records, sequence length, and sequence content.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The lab applies quality checks based on the type of sequencing data.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Check the read count and the main quality values before moving ahead.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The lab shows which analyses can be used with the dataset and why.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:05.000
View the main microbial groups in the sample and their relative abundance.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Select a phylum to see the species classified within it.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Functional potential is based on the organisms identified in the sample; it is not the same as directly detecting a gene.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
See the main microbial groups linked with each stage of the process.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Use the simulator to see how the model responds under different conditions.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Check the starting values for biogas yield, methane content, and stability.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Lower the pH and see how the simulated digester responds.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Look at how the yield and methane values change. These are simulation results, not real-plant predictions.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Use the assessment to check what you understood from the workflow.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.000
After completing the assessment, you can unlock the next level.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Moderate Mode is unlocked after assessment. Advanced Mode is available separately.
